4. **The reading** (new `packages/escher-driver/src/canvas.rs`, its unit tests in the `#[path]` child
   `canvas_tests.rs`, arch S3).
   - `Session::canvas(&mut self, id: &str) -> Result<CanvasReading, Refusal>`:
     - resolves `id` through `resolve` as `Session::layout` does, refusing `stale` or `not-found`;
     - then refuses `Cause::FontsUnavailable` where `can_paint_text` reads false, before anything is painted (a glyph
       run's text would be skipped, as a shot's would be: design-system · decision/screenshot-never-skips-text);
     - then reads `Harness::canvas_scene`.
     - It runs no step and opens no span of its own.
   - `CanvasReading` is `#[non_exhaustive]` and holds:
     - `canvas` — whether the element holds a widget whose content box is not empty: the scene was read;
     - `width` and `height` — its content box in CSS px (the border box less border and padding, floored at 0, from
       `final_layout`);
     - `commands`, a list of `CanvasCommand`, in paint order;
     - `fonts` and `images` — the 64-bit FNV-1a digests of each distinct font's and image's bytes, in first-use order;
       a command names a font or an image by its index there (F4 A).
     - An element with no widget reads `canvas: false`, a zero size and no command or resource.
   - `CanvasCommand` is `#[non_exhaustive]`, one variant per `RenderCommand` kind, holding closed values and numbers
     only:
     - `Layer` — alpha, blend mix and compose, fill rule, transform, clip path, and whether a filter or a backdrop
       filter is set; a filter's parameters are not read, a stated limit;
     - `Clip` — transform, clip path;
     - `Mask` — mode, transform, clip path;
     - `Pop`;
     - `Fill` — fill rule, brush, brush transform, transform, shape path;
     - `Stroke` — width, join, start and end caps, miter limit, dashes and dash offset, brush, brush transform,
       transform, shape path;
     - `Glyphs` (F3 A) — font index, font size, brush, brush alpha, transform, the glyph count, the box of its glyph
       origins (least x, least y, greatest x, greatest y) and the FNV-1a 64 digest of its glyph ids' little-endian
       `u32` bytes. Never a glyph id, a glyph position or text;
     - `Shadow` — transform, box, corner radii, offset, spread, deviation, colour and kind.
   - A brush is a closed value:
     - a solid colour as RGBA8;
     - a gradient's kind with its stops, each an offset and an RGBA8 colour;
     - an image by its index;
     - the words `resource` and `pattern` for the two brushes it does not read.
   - A path is its elements: move, line, quad, cubic, close, with their points. A transform is its six coefficients.
   - The digest is the kept check's hand-written FNV-1a 64 (architecture · contract/kept-check/digest), reused, never
     a second copy.
   - No `NodeId` is held or crosses (architecture · decision/no-node-id-across-session).
   - Unit tests in `canvas_tests.rs` build `Scene`s by hand:
     - one per command kind and brush kind, each table counting its rows (tests S4);
     - two runs of one font's glyphs at one index;
     - an empty scene;
     - glyph ids changed changes the digest and nothing else.

5. **The verb's row** (`packages/escher-driver/src/schema.rs`, `schema/spec.rs`, `schema_tests.rs`).
   - `pub(crate) const CANVAS: VerbSpec` after `LAYOUT` at `Level::Instance`. Its arguments:
     - `id` — required, `ArgKind::Id`;
     - `full` — optional, `ArgKind::Flag`;
     - `part` — optional, `ArgKind::Part`.
     - No new argument kind (architecture · contract/argument-kinds/flag; F8 A).
   - Its help, in the table's prose like `GRAPH`'s, states:
     - the summary by default, the full dump with `full`;
     - a `part` reads the full dump's part, `full` or not;
     - one line per command in paint order, a layer's commands indented under it and closed by `pop`;
     - numbers rounded to 1/1000;
     - no text: a glyph run's count, origins' box and ids digest;
     - fonts and images by index and digest;
     - the parts of whole lines within 10,000 bytes, `fonts` and `images` in part 1 alone, a part past the last empty;
     - `canvas: false` for an element with no widget;
     - it runs no step and changes nothing;
     - a filter's parameters are not read;
     - a command has no identity of its own, so a changed command reads in a line diff as one line removed and one
       added (architecture · decision/measured-limits-stated-in-the-tool).
   - Its result fields, each with its help:
     - `canvas` — `FieldKind::Flag`, `always: true`;
     - `width`, `height` — a new `FieldKind::Length`, summary alone;
     - `kinds` — a new `FieldKind::CommandCounts`, summary alone;
     - `depth` — `FieldKind::Count`, summary alone;
     - `digest` — a new `FieldKind::Digest`, summary alone;
     - `text` — a new `FieldKind::Commands`, full alone;
     - `fonts`, `images` — a new `FieldKind::Digests`, full alone;
     - `part`, `parts` — `FieldKind::Count`, a part alone.
   - `FieldKind` goes from seventeen kinds to twenty-two, each doc'd.
   - `VERBS` takes `CANVAS` after `LAYOUT`: sixteen verbs. Its doc (schema.rs:749) reads «the twelve verbs asked of the
     held instance».
   - In `schema_tests.rs`:
     - `the_fifteen_verbs_are_named_in_order_each_at_its_level` is renamed `…_sixteen_…`, its count and order pinned
       as literals;
     - the field-kind count and the fields-table row for `canvas` are pinned beside `layout`'s (tests S4).

6. **The command** (`packages/escher-driver/src/command.rs`, `command_tests.rs`).
   - `Command::Canvas { id: String, full: bool, part: Option<u32> }` with its doc, its `spec()` arm and a `validate`
     arm.
   - Rows in the existing tables, each table asserting its row count (tests S4):
     - accepted with an id alone, with `full`, and with `part`;
     - refused `malformed`:
       - with no id;
       - with an id past `MAX_ID_BYTES`;
       - with a part of 0 or 1001;
       - with an argument the verb does not take;
       - with `full` given twice.

8. **The written form** (`packages/escher-driver/src/json.rs`, `json_tests.rs`; F2 A). Hand-written, no serialization
   crate (architecture · decision/hand-written-answers).
   - **The summary:** `{"canvas":…,"width":…,"height":…,"kinds":{"layer":n,"clip":n,"mask":n,"pop":n,"fill":n,"stroke":n,"glyphs":n,"shadow":n},"depth":n,"digest":"<16 lowercase hex>"}`.
   - **The full dump:** `{"canvas":…,"text":…,"fonts":["<16 hex>",…],"images":["<16 hex>",…]}`, and a part adds
     `"part":n,"parts":m`. `text` is the lines, each ended by `\n`. Each line is indented two spaces per open layer, a
     part's from its `depth`.
   - **One line per command,** a fixed word then `key=value` pairs, in this order:
     - `layer alpha= blend= fill= t= clip=`, then ` filter` and ` backdrop` when set;
     - `clip t= clip=`;
     - `mask mode= t= clip=`;
     - `pop`;
     - `fill fill= brush= bt= t= shape=`;
     - `stroke w= join= cap= miter= dash= brush= bt= t= shape=`;
     - `glyphs font= size= brush= alpha= t= n= at= ids=`;
     - `shadow t= box= radii= offset= spread= dev= colour= kind=`.
   - **The values:**
     - a number rounded to 1/1000 and written shortest, `-0` as `0`, a non-finite number as `null`;
     - a transform as `id` or six numbers joined by `,`;
     - a path as SVG letters `M` `L` `Q` `C` `Z` with their numbers;
     - a colour as `#rrggbbaa`;
     - a gradient as `linear` · `radial` · `sweep` then `:` and its stops `offset#rrggbbaa` joined by `,`;
     - an image brush as `image:` and its index;
     - the words `resource` and `pattern`;
     - `bt=` and `dash=` written only when set;
     - `alpha=` only when it is not 1;
     - `ids=` the 16-hex digest.
   - Every word is kebab-case. A non-exhaustive engine set's unknown member is written by a fallback word, never a
     panic (CLAUDE.md, «No panic path on untrusted input»).
   - A `text` part's lines and the `fonts` list are the only places resources are named. No family name, font byte,
     glyph id or text is written (F3 A, F4 A).
   - **Unit tests** in `json_tests.rs`, each table counting its rows (tests S4):
     - every kind's line and every brush form written once from a hand-built reading, one whole summary and one whole
       full answer pinned as literal lines;
     - a part's indentation from its `depth`.

